   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Murray and fellow secr-users,<div><br></div><div>Potentially going to ask the simplest question on here ;) How do I stop the following warning message when using <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">plot.capthist</font> with<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> tracks=TRUE</font>?</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,serif;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.075)\">track for repeat detections on same occasion joins points in arbitrary sequence</span><br></div><div><br></div><div>I couldn&#39;t see this referenced in the help file (or on here), apologises if I have missed something obvious. </div><div><br></div><div>Alternatively, this could be an Rmarkdown chunk command (tried setting warnings=FALSE and that didn&#39;t help. Would prefer a solution within plot.capthist rather than using <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">suppressWarnings()</font>). </div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div><br></div><div>Jo</div><table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco,monospace;font-size:12px;font-variant-ligatures:normal;background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.075)\"><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:1.45;vertical-align:top;font-size:9pt!important\"><table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"font-size:13px;font-family:&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,serif\"><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"line-height:1.45;vertical-align:top;font-size:9pt!important\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><br><br></div></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ea_8CBIWCAAJ",
   "from": "Murray Efford",
   "author": "118cea91a1619106",
   "date": "2020-07-28T07:38:29Z",
   "subject": "Re: suppress warnings in plot.capthist?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>It&#39;s a true &#39;warning&#39; so can be suppressed like any other. I think the message is suppressed in RMarkdown if the chunk has warning=FALSE (not warnings=FALSE). Small difference!<br></div><div>M<br> </div></div>"
    ],
